{% set local_problem %}
<p>Cullman's established neighborhoods feature mature trees producing significant debris. Pine needles accumulate throughout the year — not just fall. Oak and maple leaves fall heavily in autumn. Seeds and pollen add to spring accumulation. Without regular cleaning, this debris clogs gutters and prevents proper water flow.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, water overflows. In North Alabama's 54+ inches of annual rainfall, that's a lot of water going where it shouldn't — pooling around foundations, soaking into fascia boards, and eroding carefully maintained landscaping.</p>

<p>For homeowners maintaining their properties to Cullman's standards, clogged gutters undermine that care. Regular professional cleaning ensures your gutters function properly and your home stays protected.</p>

<p><strong>The math:</strong> Foundation repair in Cullman County runs $10,000-30,000 depending on severity. Annual gutter cleaning runs $250-400 total (two cleanings). We've watched homeowners skip cleanings to save money, then spend five figures fixing foundation cracks. Don't learn this lesson the expensive way.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our cleaning service is thorough, not rushed.</p>

<p><strong>Step 1: Hand removal.</strong> We pull all debris from gutter troughs by hand — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter. We don't blow it onto your lawn or push it toward downspouts (a common shortcut that just moves the problem). We bag it and haul it away.</p>

<p><strong>Step 2: Downspout flush.</strong> Every downspout gets flushed with water until it runs clear. Downspout clogs are the #1 thing homeowners miss during DIY cleaning. Debris backs up in the downspout, water can't exit, and gutters overflow even though they look clean from above. If you hire someone and they don't flush downspouts, you're not getting complete service.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3: Inspection.</strong> While we're up there, we check for: loose or missing hangers, seam separations, small leaks, rust spots, and fascia showing early damage. We press on fascia to check for soft spots, not just look at it. We document problems and let you know — no scare tactics, just honest assessment.</p>

<p><strong>Step 4: Cleanup.</strong> When we leave, your property looks the same or better. No debris on the lawn, no mess in the landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters in Cullman County for over 20 years. We do thorough work, show up when scheduled, and treat your property with the respect it deserves. Nothing fancy — just reliable professional service that actually solves the problem.</p>

<p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> If you hire someone for gutter cleaning and they don't flush your downspouts, you're not getting complete service. Debris compacts into partial clogs that restrict flow — and you can't see them from above. Ask specifically. Some companies skip this step because it takes extra time. We don't.</p>

<p><strong>Our recommendation:</strong> For most Cullman homes, schedule cleanings in late November (after leaves drop) and late April (after spring pollen/seeds). If you have heavy pine coverage, add one in August. Or consider gutter guards if you're tired of the ongoing expense — they typically pay for themselves within 3 years.</p>
{% endset %}
